  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 泉\ntitle: spring; water source\njlpt: 2\ntags: [jlpt-n2, grade-6, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 9\nradical: 水\nradicalNumber: 85\nonyomi: [セン]\nkunyomi: [いずみ]\ndistractors: [原, 白, 百]\n---\n\n# 泉 — spring; water source\n\n**Strokes:** 9 · **Key (radical):** 水 (no. 85) · **JLPT:** N2 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n泉 concerns a spring or source of water. The native noun 泉 is いずみ. [温泉](../words/温泉.md) おんせん means a hot spring and can also name a hot-spring resort.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** Notice 白 above 水 and imagine clear water emerging from the ground. This is a modern-shape memory aid, not a historical derivation.\n\nThe source indexes 泉 under 水, no. 85. The water-shaped part is below 白, not a left-hand 氵.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| セン | on | [温泉](../words/温泉.md) おんせん - hot spring |\n| いずみ | kun | [泉](../words/泉.md) いずみ - spring; source of water |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [泉](../words/泉.md) いずみ - spring; source of water\n- [温泉](../words/温泉.md) おんせん - hot spring; hot-spring resort\n\n## Notes\n\n- 泉 does not say that the water is hot or safe to drink. 温泉 supplies the hot-spring word; do not infer those properties from 泉 alone.\n- English spring also names the season. That season is [春](春.md), not the water-source meaning of 泉.\n- The linked noun article distinguishes a natural water source from an ornamental spraying fountain. English fountain is not a license to replace every 噴水 ふんすい with 泉.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-21 snapshot. Word pairs: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1183450, 1390780.\n",
